        <owl:annotatedTarget>Clavulanic acid is a beta-lactamase inhibitor (marketed by GlaxoSmithKline, formerly Beecham) combined with penicillin group antibiotics to overcome certain types of antibiotic resistance. It is used to overcome resistance in bacteria that secrete beta-lactamase, which otherwise inactivates most penicillins.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:879738</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
