            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>AcrAB-TolC is a tripartite RND efflux system that confers resistance to tetracycline, chloramphenicol, ampicillin, nalidixic acid, and rifampin  in Gram-negative bacteria. The system spans the cell membrane (AcrB) and the outer-membrane (TolC), and is linked together in the periplasm by AcrA.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>AcrAB-TolC</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
