    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000457 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000457">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000115"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000001"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000103"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000023"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>ParE is a subunit of topoisomerase IV, which decatenates and relaxes DNA to allow access to genes for transcription or translation. Point mutations in ParE prevent anticoumarin antibiotics from inhibiting DNA synthesis, thus conferring resistance.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3000457</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>aminocoumarin resistant parE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000457"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ParE is a subunit of topoisomerase IV, which decatenates and relaxes DNA to allow access to genes for transcription or translation. Point mutations in ParE prevent anticoumarin antibiotics from inhibiting DNA synthesis, thus conferring resistance.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:16127057</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000458 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000458">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000201"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000056"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000208"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Macrolide glycosyltransferases are enzymes encoded by macrolide glycosyltransferase genes and inactivate macrolides by glycosylating them at 2&apos;-OH of desosamine sugar moiety. They are predominantly found in macrolide producers and are also found in non-producers and are used as a resistance mechanism. Different variants of this enzyme has been reported.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3000458</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>macrolide glycosyltransferase</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000458"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Macrolide glycosyltransferases are enzymes encoded by macrolide glycosyltransferase genes and inactivate macrolides by glycosylating them at 2&apos;-OH of desosamine sugar moiety. They are predominantly found in macrolide producers and are also found in non-producers and are used as a resistance mechanism. Different variants of this enzyme has been reported.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:17376874</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000459 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000459">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000082"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Biosynthesis of fosfomycin.</obo:IAO_0000115>
