        <obo:IAO_0000115>Chlortetracycline was an early, first-generation tetracycline antibiotic developed in the 1940&apos;s. It inhibits bacterial protein synthesis by binding to the 30S subunit of bacterial ribosomes, preventing the aminoacyl-tRNA from binding to the ribosome.</obo:IAO_0000115>
