        <owl:annotatedTarget>RmtC is a rRNA methyltransferase found in Proteus mirabilis with high level resistance to similar to aminoglycosides, with the exception of non-4,6-disubstituted deoxystreptamines (streptomycin and neomycin). It has also been isolated in Salmonella enterica ser. Virchow. It is hypothesized to methylate G1405, like related methyltransferases RmtA, RmtB, and ArmA.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:16377684</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
