        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3001310"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Phenelfamycin E was isolated from two environmental isolates called AB999F-80 and AB1047T-33. They were both identified as Streptomyces violaceoniger strains. Both these strains were found to produce phenelfamycins A-F and unphenelfamycin. Phenelfamycin E has a trisaccaride moeity and is isomeric with phenelfamycin F. All phenelfamycins were selected due to their activity against anaerobic bacteria, especially Clostridioides difficile. Phenelfamycin E and F are the most potent of the phenelfamycins.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CHEBI:222034</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
