            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>MprF is a integral membrane protein that modifies the negatively-charged phosphatidylglycerol on the membrane surface of both Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria. This confers resistance to cationic peptides that disrupt the cell membrane, including defensins. Mutations in mprF can additionally confer resistance to daptomycin in S. aureus.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3003091</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>daptomycin resistant mprF</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
