        <obo:IAO_0000115>Lipid III is the precursor to the wall teichoic acid. It&apos;s inhibition leads to bacterial death as teichoic acid is required to anchor autolysins which control the hydrolysis of peptidoglycan cell wall.</obo:IAO_0000115>
