        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>CfrA is a chloramphenicol-florfenicol resistance gene and methyltransferase enzyme. Methylation of position 8 of A2503 in 23S rRNA confers resistance to chloramphenicol antibiotics first identified by Schwarz 2000 as cfr from Mammaliicoccus sciuri. Additional Oxazolidinone resistance mediated by the cfr gene in a human isolated was first reported from Colombia in linezolid- and methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>cfr</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>cfr(A)</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>cfrA</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3003441</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>cfrA</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
