        <obo:IAO_0000115>Mycobacterium tuberculosis ethA (Rv3854c) is a mono-oxygenase enzyme which activates the antibiotic ethionamide in vivo. Mutations in ethA confer resistance to ethionamide by modulating the activation and activity of the ethionamide prodrug.</obo:IAO_0000115>
