            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>kasA is a  ketoacyl acyl carrier protein synthase that catalyzes the condensation reaction of fatty acid synthesis by the addition to an acyl acceptor of two carbons from malonyl-ACP. It is involved in elongation of fatty acids intermediate in the biosynthetic pathway of mycolic acids.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3003462</oboInOwl:id>
