        <owl:annotatedTarget>Formicin is a two-component broad-spectrum lantibiotic produced by Bacillus paralicheniformis APC 1576, exhibiting antimicrobial activity against several Gram-positive species, including Staphylococcus aureus, Clostridioides difficile and Listeria monocytogenes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
