        <owl:annotatedTarget>Ceftiofur is a third-generation broad spectrum cephalosporin and beta-lactam antibiotic predominantly used in veterinary medicine. It causes cell lysis by disrupting peptidoglycan cross-linkage and cell wall formation by binding to PBPs.</owl:annotatedTarget>
