        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_1000003"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A class of antibiotics used to treat specifically Mycobacterium tuberculosis infection; therefore, referred to as an antimycobacterial. Diarylquinoline antibiotics inhibit ATP synthesis in tuberculosis cells by disruption of mycobacterial ATP synthase.</obo:IAO_0000115>
