        <obo:IAO_0000115>ADC beta-lactamases, also known as AmpC beta-lactamases, are cephalosporinases with extended-spectrum resistance to cephalosporins and may or may not cause resistance to carbapenems. ADC beta-lactamases are found in Acinetobacter sp. and Oligella urethralis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
