        <obo:IAO_0000115>Streptomyces venezuelae rox is a class A flavoprotein monooxygenase that confers resistance to rifamycin antibiotics. It acts by oxygenating the naphthyl group of the antibiotic, leading to a ring opening event and linearization of the molecule.</obo:IAO_0000115>
