    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007779 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007779">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009657"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Three new cyclopeptides, including halolitoralin A (a cyclic hexapeptide), halolitoralin B and C (two cyclic tetrapeptides), were isolated from Halobacillus litoralis YS3106. They are likely non-ribosomal peptide antibiotics based on chemical structure, but the biosynthetic gene cluster is unknown.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3007779</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>halolitoralin</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007779"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Three new cyclopeptides, including halolitoralin A (a cyclic hexapeptide), halolitoralin B and C (two cyclic tetrapeptides), were isolated from Halobacillus litoralis YS3106. They are likely non-ribosomal peptide antibiotics based on chemical structure, but the biosynthetic gene cluster is unknown.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34677431</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007780 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007780">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007779"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Halolitoralin A is an alanine-rich cyclic hexapeptide. It exhibits potent activity against the pathogenic fungi Candida albicans and Trichophyton mentagrophytes and the gram negative bacteria Pseudomonas aeruginosa and Escherichia coli. Gram negative bacteria were found to be more sensitive than gram positive bacteria. It was also found to exhibit moderate anthelmintic activity against the earthworms Megascoplex konkanensis and Eudrilus sp.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CHEBI:207984</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PubChem:139588131</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3007780</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>halolitoralin A</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007780"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Halolitoralin A is an alanine-rich cyclic hexapeptide. It exhibits potent activity against the pathogenic fungi Candida albicans and Trichophyton mentagrophytes and the gram negative bacteria Pseudomonas aeruginosa and Escherichia coli. Gram negative bacteria were found to be more sensitive than gram positive bacteria. It was also found to exhibit moderate anthelmintic activity against the earthworms Megascoplex konkanensis and Eudrilus sp.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34677431</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


