    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009238 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009238">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009309"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The Mrr1 gene is specifically associated with the activation of the MDR1 efflux transporter. In fungi, mutations in this gene result in antifungal resistance in some fungi.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009238</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>antifungal-resistant mrr</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009239 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009239">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009299"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007508"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009363"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The Mrr2 gene encodes a zinc-cluster transcription factor that is specifically associated with the activation of the MDR1 multi-drug efflux transporter.  In fungi, mutations in this gene result in overexpression of MDR1 and potential azole resistance. Some evidence also suggests that it may influence the activation of other efflux pumps as well in Candida species.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009239</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>Candida albicans mrr2 with mutations associated with resistance to fluconazole</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009239"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The Mrr2 gene encodes a zinc-cluster transcription factor that is specifically associated with the activation of the MDR1 multi-drug efflux transporter.  In fungi, mutations in this gene result in overexpression of MDR1 and potential azole resistance. Some evidence also suggests that it may influence the activation of other efflux pumps as well in Candida species.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40790106</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009240 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009240">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009424"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>In fungi, the Tac1 gene is a zinc cluster transcription factor that influences the transcription of several proteins related to antifungal resistance. Of particular note, Tac1 influences the expression of CDR1 and CDR2 which are multi-drug efflux transporters.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009240</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>antifungal resistant TAC1</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009241 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009241">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009298"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007508"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002213"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009425"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002213"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009440"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002213"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009441"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>In fungi, the Tac1 gene is a zinc cluster transcription factor that influences the transcription of several proteins related to antifungal resistance. Of particular note, Tac1 influences the expression of CDR1 and CDR2 which are multi-drug efflux transporters. Mutations to Tac1 can result in resistance against azole drugs. These types of mutations are noted to cause a loss of heterozygosity in TAC1 through mitotic recombination of the left arm of Chromosome 5.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009241</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>Candida albicans TAC1 with mutations conferring resistance to fluconazole</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009242 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009242">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009624"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007508"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009626"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Erg3 is a distinct member of the P450 class of enzymes that encodes C-5 sterol desaturase that functions in the late ergosterol biosynthesis pathway in fungi. It catalyzes the introduction of a C-5,6 double bond into episterol and is localized to the ER membrane. Azole-mediated inhibition of Erg11 causes accumulation of toxic 14-alpha-methylated sterol intermediates and Erg3 acts on these intermediates to produce the species that are toxic to the cell. Loss-of-function mutations in ERG3 therefore confer azole tolerance by preventing the conversion of these intermediates into their toxic form, allowing the cell to survive drug exposure despite compromised ergosterol synthesis. There may be a fitness cost due to simultaneous compromises to membrane composition.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009242</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>Candida parapsilosis Erg3 C-5 sterol desaturase with mutations conferring resistance to fluconazole</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009243 -->

