                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009163"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Dihydrofolate Reductase (DHFR) is an enzyme integral to nucleotide and protein synthesis for eukaryotic life inclusive of fungi. This enzyme is targeted by certain drugs to to halt nucleotide synthesis and killing the target eukaryotic cell. Some of these drugs are useful against fungal infections, but mutations to this gene can lead to resistance against such intervention.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009290</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>Pneumocystis jerovecii dhfr with mutations associated with resistance to Trimethoprim sulfamethoxazole combined with Pyrimethamine atovaquone</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009291 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009291">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009309"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009188"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The MFS family of genes in fungi are part of the Major Facilitator Superfamily efflux pumps which are responsible for the export of antifungal compounds across the cell membrane. Mutations to this family of genes can result in anti-fungal resistance inclusive of a protein synthesis inhibiting compound like cyclohexamide.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009291</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>Trychophyton rubrum MFS1 with mutations conferring resistance against cyclohexamide</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009292 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009292">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009424"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>HapE codes for a transcription factor typically associated with cellular adaptation and is found within fungi. Mutations in this gene have been associated with resistance against several different antifungal compounds.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009292</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>antifungal-resistant HapE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009293 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009293">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009292"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>HapE codes for a transcription factor typically associated with cellular adaptation and is found within fungi. Mutations in this gene have been associated with resistance against several different antifungal compounds, including azoles.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009293</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>azole-resistant fungal HapE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009294 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009294">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009293"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007511"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009558"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>HapE codes for a transcription factor typically associated with cellular adaptation and is found within fungi. Mutations in this gene have been associated with resistance against several different antifungal compounds, including azoles.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009294</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>Aspergillus fumigatus HapE with mutations associated with resistance to itraconazole</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009295 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009295">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009271"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000001"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007495"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The ase1 gene encodes a microtubule associated protein that is particularly involved in the mitotic spindle formation and stabilization during cell division. Alterations in cell division can often lead to major genetic adaptations, such as the development of aneuploidy. In instances where a fungi can survive a major genetic adaptation, the resultant mutant could exhibit antifungal resistance.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009295</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>azole-resistant fungal ase1</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009296 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009296">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009260"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The Mfs family of genes in fungi are responsible for a variety of transport across the cell membrane. Mutations to this family of genes can result in anti-fungal resistance, especially against azole drugs.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009296</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>azole-resistant fungal mfs</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009297 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009297">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009249"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The Mdr gene is responsible for synthesis of the ABC class of efflux pumps. Mutation in this gene can result in antifungal resistance.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009297</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>azole-resistant fungal mdr</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009298 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009298">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009240"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>In fungi, the Tac1 gene is a zinc cluster transcription factor that influences the transcription of several proteins related to antifungal resistance. Of particular note, Tac1 influences the expression of CDR1 and CDR2 which are multi-drug efflux transporters.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009298</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>azole-resistant fungal tac1</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009299 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009299">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009238"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The Mrr genes are associated with the activation of the MDR1 efflux transporter. In fungi, mutations in this gene result in antifungal resistance in some fungi.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009299</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>azole-resistant fungal mrr</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009300 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009300">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009234"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Fungal Hmg enzymes which include mutations or other modifications to confer resistance to antifungal drug compounds. The Hmg pathway has roles in steroid synthesis and metabolic function in most eukaryotes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009300</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>azole-resistant fungal Hmg</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009301 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009301">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_0000031"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Mitochondrial electron transport chain (ETC) proteins involved in the respiratory chain complex for aerobic respiration in fungal organisms. Mutations in these proteins are associated with antifungal resistance by disrupting the inhibitory effect of certain drugs, such as azoxystrobin.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009301</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>strobilurin-resistant fungal cytochrome b</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009302 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009302">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007499"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Metconazole is a triazole antifungal used to control a range of fungal infections through its role as a sterol 14alpha-demethylase inhibitor.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CAS:125116-23-6</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CHEBI:81773</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ChEMBL:CHEMBL1883512</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PubChem:86210</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009302</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>metconazole</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Metconazole is a triazole antifungal used to control a range of fungal infections through its role as a sterol 14alpha-demethylase inhibitor.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:11282607</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009303 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009303">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009621"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007516"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009313"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The fungal Erg11 enzyme is lanosterol demethylase belongs to the broader P450 family. The enzyme contributes directly to ergosterol synthesis pathway. Azoles target lanosterol demethylase thereby halting ergosterol production and ultimately compromises fungal cell membrane integrity. Mutations to Erg11 genes have been shown to inhibit azole activity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009303</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>Candida albicans Erg11 with mutations conferring resistance to clotrimazole</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009304 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009304">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009305"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Strobilurins, also known as QOI fungicides, are a group of fungicides originally isolated from the fungus Strobilurus tenacellus that inhibit mitochondrial respiration by binding to Complex III in the electron transport chain thereby disrupting the fungus&apos;s ability to produce energy.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CAS:175013-18-0</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CHEBI:78780</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ChEMBL:CHEMBL519873</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PubChem:6422843</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009304</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>pyraclostrobin</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009304"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Strobilurins, also known as QOI fungicides, are a group of fungicides originally isolated from the fungus Strobilurus tenacellus that inhibit mitochondrial respiration by binding to Complex III in the electron transport chain thereby disrupting the fungus&apos;s ability to produce energy.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:12226492</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009305 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009305">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_1000003"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Strobilurins, also known as QOI fungicides, are a group of fungicides originally isolated from the fungus Strobilurus tenacellus that inhibit mitochondrial respiration by binding to Complex III in the electron transport chain thereby disrupting the fungus&apos;s ability to produce energy.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009305</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>strobilurin fungicide</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009306 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009306">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009305"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Strobilurins, also known as QOI fungicides, are a group of fungicides originally isolated from the fungus Strobilurus tenacellus that inhibit mitochondrial respiration by binding to Complex III in the electron transport chain thereby disrupting the fungus&apos;s ability to produce energy. Benzothiostrobin is a novel strobilurin fungicide with no pubchem, chebi or chembl entries as of 08/31/25.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PubChem:102198196</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009306</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>benzothiostrobin</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009306"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Strobilurins, also known as QOI fungicides, are a group of fungicides originally isolated from the fungus Strobilurus tenacellus that inhibit mitochondrial respiration by binding to Complex III in the electron transport chain thereby disrupting the fungus&apos;s ability to produce energy. Benzothiostrobin is a novel strobilurin fungicide with no pubchem, chebi or chembl entries as of 08/31/25.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>DOI:10.1111/ppa.13372</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009307 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009307">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009305"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Kresoxim-methyl is a strobilurin fungicide for the control of scab on apples and pears and other fungal diseases on a wide range of crops. It has a role as a mitochondrial cytochrome-bc1 complex inhibitor.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CAS:143390-89-0</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CHEBI:2962</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ChEMBL:CHEMBL203191</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PubChem:6112114</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009307</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>kresoxim-methyl</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009307"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Kresoxim-methyl is a strobilurin fungicide for the control of scab on apples and pears and other fungal diseases on a wide range of crops. It has a role as a mitochondrial cytochrome-bc1 complex inhibitor.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:8206295</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:8206296</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:9850581</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009308 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009308">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007499"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>1-(2-fluorophenyl)-1-(4-fluorophenyl)-2-(1H-1,2,4-triazol-1-yl)ethanol (flutriafol) is a triazole antifungal used as a fungicide in agricultural applications.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CAS:76674-21-0</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CHEBI:83707</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ChEMBL:CHEMBL2136951</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PubChem:91727</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009308</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>flutriafol</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009308"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>1-(2-fluorophenyl)-1-(4-fluorophenyl)-2-(1H-1,2,4-triazol-1-yl)ethanol (flutriafol) is a triazole antifungal used as a fungicide in agricultural applications.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:10879820</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009309 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009309">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_0010002"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>MFS is one of the two major subtypes of fungal efflux pumps that is associated with conferring antifungal resistance.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009309</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>fungal MFS family</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009311 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009311">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000708"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Several compounds are used therapeutically to kill fungal cells by means of disrupting the cell cycle, either during fungal cellular mitosis or during generalised cell growth in the interphase of the cell cycle (inclusive of G1, S and G2).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009311</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>fungal cell cycle regulating protein</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009312 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009312">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000381"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3003040"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000001"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000008"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Peptidoglycan transpeptidase proteins involved in bacterial cell wall formation and which have decreased susceptibility to some beta-lactam antibiotics. These alternative transpeptidases are found in certain organisms, like Staphylococcus aureus, and have lower affinity for penicillin-like antibiotics, such as methicillin. In these organisms, these proteins do not bind to the beta-lactam ring and therefore transpeptidase activity continues in the presence of beta-lactams, thereby conferring resistance to these drugs. These proteins are commonly clinically associated with methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009312</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>PBP2-like beta-lactam resistant peptidoglycan transpeptidase</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009313 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009313">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009195"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>In fungi, ERG11 is a gene within the CYP51 family of P450 genes. It encodes for 14 - alpha - demethylase which is an essential enzyme in the ergosterol synthesis pathway. For many fungi, ergosterol is a vital component of the cell membrane and disrupting ergosterol synthesis can halt fungal growth or even kill the fungi.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Cyp51</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009313</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>antifungal susceptible ERG11 lanosterol-14-alpha-demethylase</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009314 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009314">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000709"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Beta-1,3-glucan synthase is utilised by fungi in their cell wall synthesis. Echinocandins are a group of anti-fungal compounds that inhibit this pathway, thereby combating a fungal infection.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009314</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>antifungal-susceptible beta-1,3-glucan synthase</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009315 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009315">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009656"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Klebsazolicin is a peptide antibiotic encoded by and identified from the genome of Klebsiella pneumoniae. Klebsazolicin is a ribosomally synthesized and post-translationally modified peptide with antibiotic activity against gram-negative bacteria. Klebsazolicin inhibits ribosomal protein synthesis through binding and thus blocking peptide access.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PubChem:146684557</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>KLB</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009315</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>klebsazolicin</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009315"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Klebsazolicin is a peptide antibiotic encoded by and identified from the genome of Klebsiella pneumoniae. Klebsazolicin is a ribosomally synthesized and post-translationally modified peptide with antibiotic activity against gram-negative bacteria. Klebsazolicin inhibits ribosomal protein synthesis through binding and thus blocking peptide access.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:28846667</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009316 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009316">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009301"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Mutations conferred to the cytochrome b gene conferring resistance against strobilurin pesticides such as azoxystrobin.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009316</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>Mycosphaerella fijiensis cytochrome b protein with mutations associated with resistance to Azoxystrobin</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009317 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009317">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_1000003"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Benzimidazoles are an antibiotic class that is structurally characterized by fused imidazole and benzene rings. They act by inhibiting beta-tubulin, which is essential to the cytoskeletal structures. They are shown to exhibit antifungal activity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009317</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>benzimidazole antifungal</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009318 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009318">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_0000031"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Beta-tubulin is integral to most cellular cytoskeletal structures, including fungi. Beta tubulin is the target of benzimidazole compounds.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009318</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>antifungal-resistant beta-tubulin</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009319 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009319">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009318"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Mutated beta-tubulin genes in fungi that are resistant against benzimidazole.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009319</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>benzimidazole resistant beta-tubulin</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


