    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009323 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009323">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_1000003"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Carbamtes are a class of fungicides that target tubulin in cell cytoskeletons. This class of pesticides works similarly to benzimidazoles but is structurally different.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009323</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>carbamate fungicides</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009324 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009324">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009325"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009179"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009322"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Diethofencarb is a member of the carbamate pesticide class that targets beta tubulin within the cellular cytoskeleton of fungi. Mutations within beta-tubulin genes can confer resistance against carbamates.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009324</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>botrytis cinerea beta-tubulin with mutations conferring resistance against diethofencarb</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009324"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Diethofencarb is a member of the carbamate pesticide class that targets beta tubulin within the cellular cytoskeleton of fungi. Mutations within beta-tubulin genes can confer resistance against carbamates.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:18944187</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009325 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009325">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009318"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Carbamate fungicides target beta tubulin in fungi. Mutations within beta-tubulin genes can confer resistance against carbamates.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009325</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>carbamate resistant beta tubulin</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009326 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009326">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009328"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009188"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009327"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>ACT1 in eukaryotes fungi is associated with actin in the cytoskeletal structure. It should not be confused with ACT genes responsible for bacterial functions like beta lactamase activity. Mutations in eukaryotic ACT1 can cause conformational changes to cellular structure and can result in resistance against several compounds.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009326</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>Saccharomyces cerevisiae ACT1 with mutations conferring resistance to cycloheximide</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009327 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009327">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009321"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Actin is a part of the cytoskeleton in most cellular life, inclusive of eukaryotes like fungi.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009327</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>antifungal susceptible actin</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009328 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009328">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_0000031"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Actin is a component within cellular cytoskeletons, including eukaryotes like fungi.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009328</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>antifungal resistant actin</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009329 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009329">
