                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009348"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>ATP1 and 2 are mitochondrial enzymes linked to ATP production. Their disruption has been shown to confer resistance to azole drugs like clotrimazole.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009350</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>Saccharomyces cerevisiae ATP2 with mutations conferring resistance to clotrimazole</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009350"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ATP1 and 2 are mitochondrial enzymes linked to ATP production. Their disruption has been shown to confer resistance to azole drugs like clotrimazole.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40790106</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009351 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009351">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007115"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Fungi have a unique capacity to change their morphological structure as a means of adapting to their environment. These shifts between morphological states, such as changing between yeast and hyphae may contribute to a fungal species ability to showcase antifungal resistance.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009351</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>fungal morphological transition regulation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009352 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009352">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009564"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009353"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002213"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009566"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Byca is a suppressor of the cAMP-PKA pathway. When the PKA pathway is unrestricted, it enables the transition from yeast (avirulent) to hyphal state (filamentous, virulent). Inhibiting calcineurin through a compound like tacrolimus was thought to be a good pharmaceutical target but there are now instances of mutations that cause resistances against calcineurin inhibitors.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009352</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>Mucor circinelloides BycA with mutations conferring resistance against tacrolimus</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009353 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009353">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009165"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>tacrolimus is an immunosuppressive agent that inhibits calcineurin. This mechanism has been explored for treatment of certain fungal infections, especially mucor species.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CAS:104987-11-3</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ChEMBL:CHEMBL269732</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PubChem:445643</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009353</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>tacrolimus</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009353"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>tacrolimus is an immunosuppressive agent that inhibits calcineurin. This mechanism has been explored for treatment of certain fungal infections, especially mucor species.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31537789</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009354 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009354">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000708"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Exploitations of energy metabolism pathways in fungi have resulted in instances of antimicrobial resistance.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009354</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>fungal energy metabolism pathway enzyme</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009355 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009355">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000708"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The majority of membrane manifestations of antifungal resistance are associated with ergosterol, but there are few instances of non-ergosterol membrane lipid synthesizing enzymes that, when exploited, confer antifungal resistance.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009355</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>fungal non-ergosterol membrane lipid synthesis enzyme</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009356 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009356">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000708"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Exploitation of the fungal membrane is a proven cause of antifungal resistance. The exploitation of this region of the cells is not just limited to lipid synthesis, but also extends to membrane lipid homeostasis regulating enzymes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009356</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>fungal membrane lipid homeostasis regulating enzyme</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009357 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009357">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000708"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>General exploitations to DNA related processes can confer antifungal resistance, inclusive of nucleotide metabolism pathways.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009357</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>fungal nucleotide metabolism pathway enzyme</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009358 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009358">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000708"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Exploitations of certain post-transcriptional modifications can confer antifungal resistance.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009358</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>fungal post-transcriptional modifying protein</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009359 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009359">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000708"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Exploitations to a fungal species physical morphological state can confer antifungal resistance. Fungi have unique mechanisms that differentiate the polarity of its physical growth on a cellular level, where different membrane portions along a single cell surface can have different polarities. This mechanism is integral to a fungi&apos;s physical conformation (hyphae, pseudohyphae etc.), and exploitations of these types of mechanisms can also confer antifungal resistance.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009359</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>fungal morphogenesis and/or polarity regulating protein</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009360 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009360">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000708"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>General exploitations to DNA related processes can confer antifungal resistance, inclusive of general genome maintenance and DNA replication.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009360</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>fungal genome maintenance and DNA replication proteins</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009361 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009361">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000708"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Exploitations of fungal apoptosis pathways can confer antimicrobial resistance.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009361</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>fungal mitochondrial apoptosis regulating protein</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009362 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009362">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000708"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Exploitations to the general functioning of fungal mitochondria can confer antifungal resistance.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009362</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>fungal mitochondrial housekeeping protein</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009363 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009363">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000708"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Exploitations of certain fungal transcription facts can confer antifungal resistance.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009363</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>fungal transcription factor</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009364 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009364">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_1000002"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Aneuploid states of fungal genomes can cause an increased presence of antifungal resistance conferring genes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009364</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>fungal aneuploidy</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009365 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009365">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007668"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>HMG CoA reductase encoding genes are responsible for steroid synthesis, inclusive of ergosterol synthesis in fungi. Disruption of these proteins can result in antifungal resistance.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009365</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>azole resistant HMG-CoA reductase</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009366 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009366">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009365"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007513"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009234"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The Hmg pathway is a primarily metabolic pathway that contributes to various functions inclusive of steroid synthesis. In fungi, the synthesis of a steroid precursor is vital to the eventual formation of ergosterol which is an integral part of the fungal cell membrane. Mutations in the Hmg gene have shown conferred resistance in certain fungi against azole drugs.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009366</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>Aspergillus fumigatus Hmg2 with mutations conferring resistance to posaconazole</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


