        <obo:IAO_0000115>MRP proteins are Mitochondrial Ribosomal Proteins encode proteins that can be found exclusively in the ribosomes within mitochondria. In addition to translation, they also play a role in metabolism. In humans, mutations in some of these proteins can result in metabolic disorders. In fungi, mutations in these proteins can confer antifungal resistance.</obo:IAO_0000115>
