            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007508"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009314"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Mutations in FKS2 are associated with modifications of the beta glucan in the fungal cell wall. As such, these mutations typically showcase increased resistance against echinocandin drugs. However, some studies have reported that some FKS2 mutations can result in increased resistance against azole drugs as well.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Nakaseomyces glabratus</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009412</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>Candida glabrata FKS2 with mutations conferring resistance to fluconazole</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009412"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Mutations in FKS2 are associated with modifications of the beta glucan in the fungal cell wall. As such, these mutations typically showcase increased resistance against echinocandin drugs. However, some studies have reported that some FKS2 mutations can result in increased resistance against azole drugs as well.</owl:annotatedTarget>
