    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009575 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009575">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009621"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007513"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009313"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The fungal Erg11 enzyme is lanosterol demethylase belongs to the broader P450 family. The enzyme contributes directly to ergosterol synthesis pathway. Azoles target lanosterol demethylase thereby halting ergosterol production and ultimately compromises fungal cell membrane integrity. Mutations to Erg11 genes have been shown to inhibit azole activity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009575</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>Candida albicans ERG11 lanosterol 14-alpha-demethylase with mutations conferring resistance to posaconazole</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009575"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The fungal Erg11 enzyme is lanosterol demethylase belongs to the broader P450 family. The enzyme contributes directly to ergosterol synthesis pathway. Azoles target lanosterol demethylase thereby halting ergosterol production and ultimately compromises fungal cell membrane integrity. Mutations to Erg11 genes have been shown to inhibit azole activity.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40790106</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009576 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009576">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_1000002"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Fungi often replicate survival enhancing genes in response to external stressors. In response to antifungals, some fungi will upregulate genes that overwhelm a compounds effects or efficacy. These could include upregulations in cell wall building genes, efflux pumps etc.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009576</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>fungal copy number variation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009577 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009577">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000000"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000056"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009576"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Fungal genes can be replicated in response to external stressors, like antifungal compounds, contributing to enhanced survival capacity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009577</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>gene contributing to antimicrobial resistance through copy number variation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


