        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000001"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007499"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000001"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007500"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Lanosterol 14 alpha demethylase is involved in a critical step in the ergosterol biosynthesis pathway. It&apos;s encoded by ERG11 (Cyp51) which is a cytochrome P450 enzyme that catalyzes the oxidative removal of the 14 alpha methyl group from lanosterol. It is the primary target of azole antifungals, which bind to the heme iron in the enzyme&apos;s active site to block substrate access. This also causes the accumulation of toxic 14 alpha methylated sterol intermediates. Resistance mediated through ERG11 typically arises via point mutations in the active site that reduce azole binding affinity without abolishing catalytic activity. Additionally, upregulation of ERG11 can overwhelm the presence of azoles.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009621</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>azole resistant fungal 14 alpha demethylase</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009622 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009622">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007522"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Lanosterol 14 alpha demethylase is involved in a critical step in the ergosterol biosynthesis pathway. It&apos;s encoded by ERG11 (Cyp51) which is a cytochrome P450 enzyme that catalyzes the oxidative removal of the 14 alpha methyl group from lanosterol.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009622</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>antifungal resistant fungal 14 alpha demethylase</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009623 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009623">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007522"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>C-5 sterol desaturase is encoded by ERG3 and is an ER-membrane localized enzyme that catalyzes the introduction of a C-5,6 double bond into episterol, as part of the late ergosterol biosynthesis pathway in fungi. Under normal physiological conditions, Erg3 plays an essential role in channeling sterol intermediates toward ergosterol, the primary sterol of fungal membranes that maintains membrane fluidity, integrity, and the function of membrane-associated proteins. When azoles inhibit Erg11, toxic 14-alpha-methylated sterol intermediates accumulate, and Erg3 acts on these intermediates to produce the species that are directly membrane-toxic to the cell. Loss-of-function mutations in ERG3 therefore confer azole tolerance by compromising this toxic conversion, allowing the cell to persist under drug pressure despite being unable to synthesize ergosterol normally.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009623</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>antifungal resistant fungal C-5 sterol desaturase</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009624 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009624">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009623"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000001"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007499"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>C-5 sterol desaturase is encoded by ERG3 and is an ER-membrane localized enzyme that catalyzes the introduction of a C-5,6 double bond into episterol, as part of the late ergosterol biosynthesis pathway in fungi. Under normal physiological conditions, Erg3 plays an essential role in channeling sterol intermediates toward ergosterol, the primary sterol of fungal membranes that maintains membrane fluidity, integrity, and the function of membrane-associated proteins. When azoles inhibit Erg11, toxic 14-alpha-methylated sterol intermediates accumulate, and Erg3 acts on these intermediates to produce the species that are directly membrane-toxic to the cell. Loss-of-function mutations in ERG3 therefore confer azole tolerance by compromising this toxic conversion, allowing the cell to persist under drug pressure despite being unable to synthesize ergosterol normally.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009624</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>azole resistant fungal C-5 sterol desaturase</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009625 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009625">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009623"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000001"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007496"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>C-5 sterol desaturase is encoded by ERG3 and is an ER-membrane localized enzyme that catalyzes the introduction of a C-5,6 double bond into episterol, as part of the late ergosterol biosynthesis pathway in fungi. Under normal physiological conditions, Erg3 plays an essential role in channeling sterol intermediates toward ergosterol, the primary sterol of fungal membranes that maintains membrane fluidity, integrity, and the function of membrane-associated proteins.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009625</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>echinocandin resistant fungal C-5 sterol desaturase</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009626 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009626">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009195"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>In fungi, C5-desaturase is usually encoded by ERG3 which is a critical enzyme in the ergosterol biosynthesis pathway. Its primary function is to catalyze the introduction of a carbon-carbon double bond at the C5 position of the sterol intermediate episterol.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009626</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>antifungal susceptible ERG3 C-5 sterol desaturase</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009627 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009627">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009624"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007514"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009626"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Erg3 is a distinct member of the P450 class of enzymes that encodes C-5 sterol desaturase that functions in the late ergosterol biosynthesis pathway in fungi. It catalyzes the introduction of a C-5,6 double bond into episterol and is localized to the ER membrane. Azole-mediated inhibition of Erg11 causes accumulation of toxic 14-alpha-methylated sterol intermediates and Erg3 acts on these intermediates to produce the species that are toxic to the cell. Loss-of-function mutations in ERG3 therefore confer azole tolerance by preventing the conversion of these intermediates into their toxic form, allowing the cell to survive drug exposure despite compromised ergosterol synthesis. There may be a fitness cost due to simultaneous compromises to membrane composition.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009627</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>Candida parapsilosis Erg3 C-5 sterol desaturase with mutations conferring resistance to isavuconazole</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009628 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009628">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000708"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Some fungi have extracellular barriers, like capsules, that contribute to their survival capacity against some environmental stressors.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009628</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>fungal extracellular capsule synthesizing enzyme</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009629 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009629">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009631"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007558"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009630"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>UXS1 encodes a UDP-xylose synthase that converts UDP-glucuronic acid to UDP-xylose for capsule biosynthesis in some fungi. When mutated, UDP-GlcUA accumulates, downregulating the permease Fcy2. Permease Fcy2 is a membrane enzyme that is required for cellular uptake of the antifungal 5-FC. UXS1 is best categorized as a fungal extracellular polysaccharide/capsule biosynthesis enzyme.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009629</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>Cryptococcus neoformans USX1 UDP-xylose synthase with mutations conferring resistance to 5-fluorocytosine</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009630 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009630">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009628"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>UDP-xylose synthase is involved the synthesis of extracellular capsules in some fungi. It also is responsible for the presence of Fcy2 enzyme in the cell membrane, which is the site of import for the antifungal 5-flucytosine.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009630</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>antifungal susceptible USX1 UDP-xylose synthase</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009631 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009631">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_0000031"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000001"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007560"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>UXS1 encodes a UDP-xylose synthase that converts UDP-glucuronic acid to UDP-xylose for capsule biosynthesis. When mutated, UDP-GlcUA accumulates, downregulating the permease Fcy2 and reducing cellular uptake of the antifungal 5-FC, conferring resistance. UXS1 is best categorized as a fungal extracellular polysaccharide/capsule biosynthesis enzyme.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009631</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>antifungal resistant USX</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009632 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009632">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_0000031"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000001"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000034"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>URA enzymes in fungi catalyze sequential steps in the de novo pyrimidine biosynthesis pathway, converting simple precursors ultimately into UMP and UDP for nucleotide synthesis. Their relevance to antifungal resistance lies in their intersection with 5-flucytosine metabolism where the compound is converted intracellularly into toxic fluorinated pyrimidine analogs that hijack the pathway.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009632</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>antifungal resistant Ura</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009633 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009633">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009632"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009160"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009634"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Uridylate kinase that catalyzes an enzymatic step in the biosynthesis of pyrimidines, converting uridine monophosphate into uridine-5 (prime)-diphosphate. It&apos;s mutation might cause the inhibition of steps involved in the production of toxic compounds derived from 5-FC.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009633</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>Cryptococcus neoformans Ura6 uridylate kinase with mutations conferring resistance to 5-fluorocytosine</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009633"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Uridylate kinase that catalyzes an enzymatic step in the biosynthesis of pyrimidines, converting uridine monophosphate into uridine-5 (prime)-diphosphate. It&apos;s mutation might cause the inhibition of steps involved in the production of toxic compounds derived from 5-FC.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40790106</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009634 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009634">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009357"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Ura6 encodes a uridylate kinase that catalyzes an enzymatic step in the biosynthesis of pyrimidines, converting uridine monophosphate into uridine-5(prime)-diphosphate.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009634</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>antifungal susceptible ura6</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009635 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009635">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009424"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>UPC2 encodes a transcription factor that is a master regulator of ergosterol biosynthesis in fungi.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009635</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>antifungal resistant Upc2</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009636 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009636">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009635"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000001"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007499"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>UPC2 encodes a transcription factor that is a master regulator of ergosterol biosynthesis in fungi. Its mutation is clinically important because gain-of-function mutations in UPC2 are a well-known mechanism of azole resistance.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009636</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>azole resistant Upc2</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009637 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009637">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009636"/>
