            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007508"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009638"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002213"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009313"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002213"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009626"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>UPC2 encodes a transcription factor that is a master regulator of ergosterol biosynthesis in fungi. Its mutation is clinically important because gain-of-function mutations in UPC2 are a well-known mechanism of azole resistance.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009637</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>Candida albicans Upc2 with mutations conferring resistance to fluconazole</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009638 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009638">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009363"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000000"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3007508"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>UPC2 encodes a transcription factor that is a master regulator of ergosterol biosynthesis in fungi. Its mutation is clinically important because gain-of-function mutations in UPC2 are a well-known mechanism of azole resistance.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009638</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>antifungal susceptible Upc2</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009639 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009639">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009363"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>In fungi, the Tac1 gene is a zinc cluster transcription factor that influences the transcription of several proteins related to antifungal resistance. Of particular note, Tac1 influences the expression of CDR1 and CDR2 which are multi-drug efflux transporters. Mutations to Tac1 can result in resistance against azole drugs. These types of mutations are noted to cause a loss of heterozygosity in TAC1 through mitotic recombination of the left arm of Chromosome 5.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009639</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>antifungal susceptible Tac1</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009640 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009640">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000451"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Gene products that regulate efflux of antibiotics from cells.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009640</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>antibiotic efflux regulatory protein</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009641 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009641">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000017"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_2000001"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3000008"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Oxacillin-hydrolyzing class D OXA beta-lactamases without assigned sub-family.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ARO:3009641</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>OXA beta-lactamase without subfamily</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009642 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_3009642">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ARO_0000000"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Nafithromycin (WCK 4873) is a lactone- ketolide antibiotic effective against respiratory pathogens.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PubChem:117587595</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>WCK 4873</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
